{"body":{"text":["The elevation is what was said, lifted so the author can look upon all of it at once and see only what matters: \"I want to be able to plot up all of the steps, put things into perspective, and from there, naturally being able to prioritize and not\" (23/50). Threads alone could not give that: \"just threads to me is a little bit of chaos, probably\" (23/50). Less is more, and each new elevation looks upon those already there (23/62). *Leaning, 23/50 to 23/138; unlike the rest of How we work, this is the author's own leaning.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA000","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["There are three levels. The ground is the sessions and their utterances, as they are kept. Knowledge stands on top, briefs written under the rule. Between them stands the elevation: \"the bottom level being the source, the discussions, the top level being the briefs, and this being the intermediate layer\" (23/94). The elevation tells what was said and where; Knowledge tells what holds and why (23/90, 23/91)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA001","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **statement** is one sentence written under the rule, saying first what it is, a second sentence allowed only for its reason (23/98, 23/129); whether one is enough the author asks, though \"I appreciate the idea that it should be\" (23/116). \"statements and everything should honor the nature of what they are, and if they are something to do, if they are a task, if they are an action, they should be named appropriately\" (23/98): a task is named as the doing, and what was objected to is written as what is held instead, as the session drew it (23/119). It has no name, being reached only through what holds it, and points at its ground, the utterances or sentences it rests on, the author's words or the session's (23/80), shown by their numbers as Knowledge shows them (23/115, 23/116)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA002","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Every statement has a **status**, where it stands now: open, asked and not decided; proposed, the session's and not taken up by the author; leaning, inclined to with doubt; settled, decided; closed, no longer holding. These are Knowledge's own marks, with closed beside them. Each status points at what gave it, the utterance of the decision, and so whose it was. A statement's history is its versions (23/132)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA003","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Closed points at what closed it, a statement, a commit, a brief or the author's word, and may be opened again: \"Knowledge is built on its grounds, and any new ground may always exist, shifting the landscape of other pieces of knowledge\" (23/138). Of the two words offered, \"Closed is probably better. It's more precise\" than set aside, which tells a reason that may be wrong and sounds softer than it is; closed is silent on its reason (23/137, 23/138)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA004","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A statement that is something to do also has **work**: to do, or done, pointing at the commit that did it. Settled is not done, since a decided fact or principle has nothing left to do (23/124, 23/125). When the work is done the statement is said again as what now holds: \"The work point about the statement being written to what now holds makes sense\" (23/132). What is planned to be built is every statement whose work is still to do."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA005","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A **topic** is a short name, holding statements: \"topics need short names because topics naturally are addressable\" (23/116). A statement stands in as many topics as it is about, and topics may hold topics, as the session answered and the author took up: \"Yeah, why not?\" (23/111, 23/112). A topic keeps its spans, the stretches of sessions where it was spoken of, each written between(session, from, to) (23/79, 23/80). Its spans are read from its statements' grounds, written by hand only where talk ran with nothing stated (23/129). A topic with nothing in Knowledge yet is, as the session put it, a debt in plain sight (23/91). Whether a topic is a brief is open (23/104 to 23/108)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA006","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Work that belongs together is gathered in a brief in Knowledge, and its order is the prose of the way from here: \"We don't need to have structured and typed data for project management\" (23/100); the groups \"can be made by briefs\" (23/116). How a brief's flow holds statements, beside paragraphs, lists, code and briefs, is open."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA007","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Threads, paths and cycles go once the sessions are drawn anew: \"Yes, threads and paths are let go, but so is more things, cycles, etc.\" (23/110). Condensations and measures go with them on the session's list, which he did not contest (23/111), though he once thought measures might be a dimension of their own (23/52). Statistics and their board stay, an idea the interface was not ready for (23/52). Values, which \"ought to be a brief somewhere anyway, probably\" (23/62), wait for that brief. Until the redraw, the threads stand as they are."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA008","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["A reader drew every session so, in files, as 48 topics and 459 statements, with a page made to look upon them (23/85 to 23/89); a final pass found 420 of the statements fitting, and the model was changed by the rest (23/129, 23/137)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA009","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["The elevation gives what, not why: the reasoning, the turns of a talk and the author's state stay in the sessions and in Knowledge (23/93)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00A","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["Knowledge is to hold all of it, so the next session works from Knowledge alone: \"the knowledge holon should contain naturally everything because it's a skill\" (23/130, 23/131). Its steps stand in the way from here."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00B","instance":["1M6YBY3G0000002"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Elevating what was said:** the types, statement and topic, written with their moulds; then three sessions, the twelfth, eighteenth and twenty-third, drawn and read back by a blank reader; then every session drawn, the work gathered into briefs and this order written over them, and threads, paths, cycles, condensations and measures let go (23/110, 23/129, 23/131, 23/138). *Leaning, 23/138; the next session's, once the author has read this (23/138).*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00C","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The author's review of the components and the chassis,** begun in the twenty-second session: the pill and the list plain, each component naming its code in its holon, the query the browser's address through the location, the components a store of their own (22/3 to 22/44); next the chassis kept apart from its renderer, each concern a file of its own (22/9, 22/10; the path The chassis apart from its renderer), and the rest of the glue. *Open: the thread The components' remaining glue.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00D","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Input, layers and overlays:** the root reserving gestures and input otherwise the components', a gesture passed up the holarchy until captured, the context menu matching over where it was pressed, and an overlay layer for it and for completion (23/23 to 23/29), with chrome, nested chassis and accessibility beside them; the git integration may come first, as the author weighs (23/27). *Open: the threads named under Components.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The old wiki's fate:** whether The wiki, kept as it stood, is let go, as the author leaned to if Knowledge holds all it does (18/105), and whether the reasoning it alone holds comes into Knowledge first. *Open, awaiting the author.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00F","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Fewer passes to the stores:** \"I would thikn it shouldn t need many passes to the store if we have the right native vocabulary\" (19/72). A brief is now read in one read, and what a read applies learned a layer at a time, each function it names asked whole (20/16, 20/34); it is still learned every read, and knowing it across reads would be the engine keeping something, a deeper discussion the author set apart: \"architecturally, that's not what we drew\" (20/11). The reads of a page run again on each move of the query, where the author holds only reads receiving a change should (21/77); re-deriving only where a change flows is, he says, \"for the future … probably a requirement of an engine\" (21/90), the successor (21/96). *Open; the thread Reads re-derived where a change flows.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00G","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The git integration:** the linked code of holons seen, the repository's tree navigable as it is, one store on the start page (19/19); read-only first, as the session proposed."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00H","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Reading git from a browser, tested:** a repository served as plain files read from a page, with no proxy and no limit, before building on it (19/24)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00J","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The stores read through git,** locally and published alike, the build no longer copying them (19/21)."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00K","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Then the threads** standing open, divergence first among them: when a commit lands in some stores it touches and misses others, the holons it wrote marked diverged, the later commit's version found to answer, and the share not delivered kept while the engine lives, as settled at 12/77. *Open: where the mark is kept, and so whether a read may then ask for a holon only where holding says it lies; the threads Where divergence is marked, Where a holon is kept and Holding links to history.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00M","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Stopping a store:** the store contract has no way to let a store go; the location listens only while subscribed, but strata keeps its files and timers (22/19, 22/20). A clear task for the near future, at the author's word (22/19). *Open: the thread Stopping a store.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00N","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Addresses through a store's identity:** an address and a dependency begin at a mount's local name, where a reference by id names no store, the two behaving differently, as the author asked and the session confirmed (22/41, 22/42). The session proposed a store's identity its root's id, addresses and dependencies to resolve through it, and following an id to whatever store holds it as right (22/40), *Proposed*; the author asked of the long run, \"Thinking about the absolute future, not a pilot phase\", and held, of a store gone and another mounted with the same holon, that \"it makes sense though that it doesn't automagically point to the new place\" (22/39). *Open: the thread Addresses through a store's identity.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00P","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**The command line able to commit,** so the field is written through the engine by hand and the author's tools in `author/` go. *The tools going, settled 2026-11-11.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00Q","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["**Holons read as the type asked,** as the buffer of characters is read as a string."]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00R","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
{"body":{"text":["*The engine, the interface and the stores were merged onto main and the site published (19/25); the expressions as uses, the buffer, the interface and the site on the engine, the stores in strata and components declared in their holons, the steps before these, are built, as each part says. The chassis was broken away at the author's word (20/19), and the components made plain functions over `io`, rendered and laid out by it (21/57, 21/72), built; the author's review of them began in the twenty-second session (22/3), the location built as the first integration and the components given a store of their own (22/44); in the twenty-third session the author considered how input, the context menu and overlays are to work, and held a card only a card (23/21, 23/29); the elevation of what was said is next (23/138), then the chassis apart from its renderer, then input, layers and overlays or the git integration (19/19, 23/27). The order is the session's. Proposed.*"]},"id":"1M89J1SGDVQA00S","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000Z"]}
